" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
"  Not carried over from the VS Code config, and why:
"
"  * Magit bindings (x, -, S--, S-o, y, g in magit buffers)
"      No Magit for the IntelliJ platform. The <leader>g menu drives the
"      built-in Git tool window instead; it covers status, commit, push,
"      pull, branches, log, blame, stash and rollback.
"
"  * The shift+s explorer macro (split down + open + close others)
"      VS Code's `runCommands` has no IdeaVim equivalent. Closest is
"      <leader>w- then opening the file.
"
"  * Suggest-widget / parameter-hint / code-action navigation
"      Handled by the IDE half of the setup, in keymaps/VSCode-Vim.xml,
"      because those popups are IDE-owned and Vim never sees the keys.
" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
